  "limitations": [
    "Provisional intervals come from in-sample development residuals and are expected to be anti-conservative; the reported 2024 coverage is the honest check on them. Calibrated intervals are an A3 deliverable.",
    "The global estimator is a regularized linear model, not gradient boosting: scikit-learn is absent from .venv and the plan forbids a new dependency without Mher's documented approval. A nonlinear learner could change the comparison against the local baseline.",
    "target_day_of_week enters as a numeric code under the frozen A1 feature contract, which a linear model cannot read as a cyclical effect.",
    "August is not read at A2. Any cross-state statement waits for A4 and needs a registry allowed_consumers entry for the vintage.",
    "Bering Strait has a zero median absolute deviation over the context window, so its context scale falls back to the standard deviation."
  ],
